{{- /*
  support/target-bead-picker — the full "Step 1: Identify the target
  bead" block used at the top of every single-bead support prompt
  (check-status, investigate, reply-to-user, gather-info).

  The block always:
    1. resolves $target from either .Session.BeadsIssue (context-menu
       launch) or .Args.IssueID (parameter form),
    2. if a target was resolved, prints the "launched from bead" line
       so the prompt operates directly on it,
    3. otherwise runs a `mitto_ui_options` picker over the open
       `support-question` beads. When a Filter is passed, the picker
       narrows the candidate universe to that state and adds an
       "if there are no such beads, notify and stop" nudge.

  The template-call syntax `{{ template "name" X }}` accepts a single
  value, so callers pass a small `dict` carrying both the ctx and the
  optional filter label:

      generic (all open questions):
          {{ template "_shared/support/target-bead-picker"
             (dict "Ctx" . "Filter" "") }}

      drafting-only:
          {{ template "_shared/support/target-bead-picker"
             (dict "Ctx" . "Filter" "state:drafting"
                   "EmptyMessage" "nothing is ready to answer") }}

      need-info-only:
          {{ template "_shared/support/target-bead-picker"
             (dict "Ctx" . "Filter" "state:need-info"
                   "EmptyMessage" "nothing is awaiting a customer detail (nothing to follow up on)") }}

  Whitespace contract identical to the other _shared fragments: body
  is column-1 Markdown, no leading/trailing newline; callers use plain
  `{{ template ... }}` (no trim markers) and rely on YAML newlines.
*/ -}}
{{- $ctx := .Ctx -}}
{{- $filter := .Filter -}}
{{- $emptyMsg := .EmptyMessage -}}
{{- $target := "" -}}
{{- if $ctx.Session.BeadsIssue }}{{ $target = $ctx.Session.BeadsIssue }}{{ else if $ctx.Args.IssueID }}{{ $target = $ctx.Args.IssueID }}{{ end -}}
{{- if $target }}
- This prompt was launched from bead **`{{ $target }}`** — operate on it directly (skip the picker).
{{- else if eq $filter "" }}
- **No linked bead** — show a picker: list open tracked questions
  `bd list -l support-question --status open,in_progress --all` (read each `state:*` label from
  `bd show`). Present them with `mitto_ui_options` (first option `{label: "None - Cancel"}`, then
  one `{label: "<id> [state] — <short summary>"}` per bead, timeout 300). If the user cancels,
  acknowledge and stop.
{{- else }}
- **No linked bead** — show a picker: list candidates and keep only those in `{{ $filter }}`:
  `bd list -l support-question --status open,in_progress --all` (read each `state:*` label from
  `bd show`). Present them with `mitto_ui_options` (first option `{label: "None - Cancel"}`, then
  one `{label: "<id> [state] — <short summary>"}` per bead, timeout 300).
- If there are no `{{ $filter }}` beads, `mitto_ui_notify` (info) that {{ if $emptyMsg }}{{ $emptyMsg }}{{ else }}nothing matches{{ end }} and stop.
  If the user cancels, acknowledge and stop.
{{- end }}
{{- /* no trailing newline */ -}}
